# =============================================================================
# CitOmni - robots.txt (DEVELOPMENT)
#
# PURPOSE
#   Prevent compliant crawlers from accessing development content.
#   Complement the HTTP noindex policy applied by the development server config.
#
# THREAT MODEL
#   - Reduce the risk of development URLs being crawled or surfaced by search engines.
#   - Prevent crawlers from traversing unfinished, temporary, or test content.
#
# BEHAVIOR
#   - "Disallow: /" blocks crawling of all paths for compliant crawlers.
#   - robots.txt controls crawling only; it is not access control and does not by
#     itself guarantee that a discovered URL will never appear in a search index.
#
# NOINDEX
#   - Do not add "Noindex:" here. It is not a supported robots.txt directive.
#   - A crawler blocked by "Disallow: /" may know that a URL exists without fetching
#     the response, so robots.txt alone is not a guarantee against index presence.
#   - Development HTTP responses use X-Robots-Tag when fetched. If an externally
#     reachable dev environment must never be indexed, use access control rather
#     than relying on robots.txt alone.
#
# NOTES
#   - Keep noindex enforcement in HTTP headers for development responses.
#   - Protect externally reachable development environments with appropriate
#     network or HTTP access controls when required.
# =============================================================================


User-agent: *
Disallow: /
